      "id": 14,
      "options": {
        "code": {
          "language": "plaintext",
          "showLineNumbers": false,
          "showMiniMap": false
        },
        "content": "**What this dashboard cannot tell you.** These are GPU-side counters. They show that *an* encode is running, not *which* item or *which* user - jellyfin does not export per-session metrics, and nothing here is scraped from it.\n\n**If the encoder is flat while playback is broken**, the GPU is not the problem. Check, in order: whether the client is direct-playing (nothing to transcode), whether the jellyfin pod has `runtimeClassName: nvidia` and the `nvidia.com/gpu` limit, and whether `nvidia.com/gpu` is allocatable at all - the Kubernetes Allocation dashboard covers the last two.",
        "mode": "markdown"
      },
